    pipeline (resolve_related_records, create_property_from_vals,
    process_feed_properties, portal_line tracking, is_feed_sourced
    compute) is schema-agnostic.

    This fixture contains 3 properties covering the realistic scenarios:

      1. Marina Heights Tower 1204 - Dubai Marina apartment, sale + lease.
         Resolves cleanly against Dubai / Dubai Marina existing records.

      2. Palm Jumeirah Villa - offplan villa, sale-only. Permit_id is
         set so the Phase 0.6 Trakheesi uniqueness constraint is exercised
         (a SECOND feed run with the same permit_number should fail with
         ValidationError on update — but update uses .write() which calls
         @api.constrains only on stored fields, so this depends on
         onchange vs constraint timing — see test_inbound_feed_service.py).

      3. Sharjah Studio - small unit, lease-only, missing some optional
         fields (no agent, no images, no permit). Tests that the parser
         is tolerant of partial feeds.
-->
